give undue weight to minor aspects of its subject but should strive to treat 
each aspect with a weight proportional to its treatment in the body of 
reliable, published material on the subject.\n8. Any inclusion of fringe or 
pseudoscientific views should not give them undue weight. The fringe or 
pseudoscientific view should be clearly described as such. An explanation of 
