the object within the wider assemblage of Late Bronze Age elite jewelry and 
sealing devices from the Argolid and Messenia, which are commonly grouped under
the label of Creto‑Mycenaean gold rings.[1][4]\n\nThe conventional association 
of the ring with the Palace of Nestor at Pylos rests partly on its Mycenaean 
